Package: bayesian.tx.temp
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Change-Point Analysis of Texas Summer Temperatures
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Campbell", "Brickhouse", email = "ctbrickhouse@tamu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Shandon", "Bringhurst", email = "shandonb@tamu.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Caleb", "Notheis", email = "Caleb.Notheis@tamu.edu", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Group project for TAMU STAT 638 (Applied Bayesian Analysis).
    Investigates whether the average summer daily maximum temperature at
    Austin Camp Mabry, TX (GHCND:USW00013958) has changed over time, and
    whether the long-term pattern is better described by a gradual trend
    or one or more abrupt change points, using Bayesian change-point
    models compared against frequentist alternatives.
